  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A rigid massless rod of length <math><mn>3</mn><mi>l</mi></math> has two masses attached at each end as shown in the figure. The rod is pivoted at point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;on the horizontal axis. When released from the initial horizontal position, its instantaneous angular acceleration will be</p><p><br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0196_bad139ff52d8.png\" style=\"width: 320px; height: 80px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>13</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0196_765025fe8ce6.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 164px;\" /><br /><br />Both the weight will produce torques in opposite directions,<br /><br />&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#964;</mi><mi>net</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;(where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>moment if inertia about axis of rotation)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>l</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>m</mi><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>l</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>13</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>"
  }
